  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Universitat Politècnica de València (UPV) is one of Spain's leading public technical universities, consistently ranked among the top technological institutions in Europe. Located in the coastal city of Valencia, UPV combines academic excellence with cutting-edge research and strong industry links. It is particularly renowned for engineering, architecture, and technology-related fields.\n\nWith over 30,000 students across its three campuses—Valencia, Gandia, and Alcoy—UPV provides an innovative and international learning environment. The university offers a wide selection of undergraduate and graduate programs, many of which are available in English, attracting students from over 100 countries.\n\nUPV is known for its commitment to sustainability, entrepreneurship, and hands-on learning, making it an ideal choice for future-focused students looking for a high-quality, affordable European education.\n\nUPV offers diverse bachelor's degree programs that combine strong theoretical foundations with applied skills. Popular English and Spanish-taught undergraduate programs include:\n\nUPV's emphasis on project-based learning and internships helps students gain real-world experience early in their studies."
